    "agent_guidance": "No Docker image or real directory/LDAP/database server is required: JNDIRealm tests mock SSL hostname verification rather than contacting a real LDAP server, JAASRealm tests use a local tomcat/jaas-realm-resource.config test resource, and JDBC-backed tests use an in-memory H2 URL. If tests are added that exercise JreCompat/classloader-leak-prevention/digester-system-property paths (mirroring JreCompatTest, JreMemoryLeakPreventionListenerTest, DigesterTest in the 11.0.x suites), add these JVM args to the javaTest task: --add-opens=java.base/java.io=ALL-UNNAMED, --add-opens=java.base/java.lang=ALL-UNNAMED, --add-opens=java.base/java.lang.reflect=ALL-UNNAMED, --add-opens=java.base/java.util=ALL-UNNAMED, --add-opens=java.rmi/sun.rmi.transport=ALL-UNNAMED, and the system property -Dorg.apache.tomcat.util.digester.PROPERTY_SOURCE=org.apache.tomcat.util.digester.SystemPropertySource. Only add the specific flags a given new test actually needs rather than copying all of them speculatively. If any such test runs under nativeTest, also set runtime arg -Djava.home=<JAVA_HOME or GRAALVM_HOME>.",
